            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Will pursue this as a state decorator on /xyz/openbmc_project/state/bmc0 at https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/82789 as by definition that  is the path for the running BMC."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "What does \"Local\" signify here?  I'm having trouble determining if \"local\" and \"bmc\" are actually necessary in the interface name here or we just use \"position\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "There is code that needs to know which BMC it is running on, i.e. 0 or 1, which we can get from a GPIO.\n\nIf it is a generic position interface, it would have to go somewhere unique like 'inventory/system' so that code could find it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Which I should add, is fine with me."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "This can also be used to know the position of the chassis as to which chassis it is in multi-chassis systems. just using the position will allow it to be used either under the system as to which chassis is the manager where the code is executing or under chassis as to which position this chassis has as well as under cards if needed like to the the BMC cards to know what position the inventory object is."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I've seen changed it to be a more generic position."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "read-only flag?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Yea, probably should be, thanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Since the desire is for this to go into phosphor-inventory-manager, it can't be read only after all."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think this is appropriate on an inventory item.  If it isn't valid or can't be determined, don't create the interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Will fix."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jinu Joy Thomas",
                        "email": "jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jinuthomas"
                    },
                    "message": "we may not need a flag we could use the position itself to determine if the position can be determined just that the type needs to be changed to a signed type."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocalBMCPosition.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
