        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "b79b344ac6117a60eea6d86f02b4b1863888431c",
            "parents": [
                "d2c73f6494f366351dc431b682e73209ef03cc50"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/02/82702/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Matt Spinler",
                "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "spinler"
            },
            "createdOn": 1755531960,
            "author": {
                "name": "Matt Spinler",
                "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                "username": "spinler"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "How is this different from https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/LocationCode.interface.yaml? Can both co-exist?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "There's also https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Slot.interface.yaml"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "IBM has a very specific use for location code already, and it's different than this.\n\nIf we have a freestanding chassis that is cabled to another chassis, does it have a slot or position?  It feels more like a 'position', though the existing slot interface would still work and if this is deemed too similar that's fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "If we are going to make this interface, can we add to the description how it is different from the `Decorator.Slot` interface.\n\nYou have your use-case in mind but others in the future will have to make a decision which one of these to use, and it should be clear from the `description` field of the interfaces.\n\nFor `LocationCode`, i understand that's different since it's a string and does not allow for straightforward ordering.\n\n> If we have a freestanding chassis that is cabled to another chassis, does it have a slot or position?\n\nIn this example, which `Position` do you assign to each one? Is there a `main` chassis which manages the other one? Does it then get Position `0`.\n\n> though the existing slot interface would still work and if this is deemed too similar that's fine.\n\nI would prefer if you could use the existing interface, if at all possible \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "> If we are going to make this interface, can we add to the description how it is different from the Decorator.Slot interface.\n\nWill do.  When I created the Slot interface a few years ago, it was to distinguish PCIe slots.\n\n> In this example, which Position do you assign to each one? Is there a main chassis which manages the other one? Does it then get Position 0.\n\n\nI already have:\n\"when it's necessary to distinguish it from other inventory items of the same type.\"\n\nI would say it's implied that a super chassis is not the same type as a sub chassis, though I will try to think of a way to enhance what I have.\n\n> I would prefer if you could use the existing interface, if at all possible\n\nIt's one of those things, do we want to be stuck with a term just because it was first.  I go back and forth."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> \"when it's necessary to distinguish it from other inventory items of the same type.\"\n\nThe Slot interface has description\n`Implement to provide a slot number for an inventory item.`\n\nLet's say i have an inventory item,\nhow would i choose one or both of those interfaces to put on it?\n\nI'm all for having this interface if it's meaningfully different and we know when to use which one.\n\nSomething else i want to understand here, can we have multiple inventory items with same inventory dbus interface and  same `SlotNumber`?\n\nAnd can we have multiple inventory items present with same inventory dbus interface and same `Position`?\n\n> If we have a freestanding chassis that is cabled to another chassis, does it have a slot or position? It feels more like a 'position', though the existing slot interface would still work and if this is deemed too similar that's fine.\n\nI believe i have similar use case for supporting multi-host systems.\n\nWhat do you think of this description\n\n```\nHolds the position of an inventory item\nwhen there are multiple instances of an inventory item with the same \nxyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Slot::SlotNumber\nsuch as in multi-host, blade server, or multi-chassis systems.\n\nIn such cases,\nthe xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator::Position\nproperty will be same as \n`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.ManagedHost::HostIndex\nproperty, if managed host interface is present.\n\nIn case of having only one instance of an inventory item with a given \nxyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator::Position, \n\nxyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Position\ndoes not imply existence of \nxyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Slot\n```\n\nThat would allow me to have some kind of workaround for multi-host hardware inventories in redfish while the associations are still being worked on.\n\nSorry for the text dump \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I think you decided to use associations for all of your multi host stuff.\n\nFor this, I'm just going update it to base it on the actual definition of a slot."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this 0-based? Or implementation defined?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I would say implementation defined.  let me know if you think that needs  to go into the YAML."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "To deal with the situation where position could not be determined due to some unknown reason, is it fine if we move away from type \"size\" to accommodate value like \"-1\" denoting that the value is invalid?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, we need a value like \"-1\" denoting that value is not determined."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "No, we don't necessarily need -1.  Use `intmax`.  You can even set that as the `default: intmax` in the YAML if you prefer."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Good idea, I'll add that as the default."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Decorator/Position.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 6,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
